WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.749
Worked examples are powerful because they let learners study a correct problem-solving pattern before they are responsible for every step.

2
00:00:08.749 --> 00:00:13.332
For beginners, unguided problem solving too early can overload working memory.

3
00:00:13.332 --> 00:00:20.831
They may spend so much effort searching for a path that little attention remains for understanding the principle.

4
00:00:20.831 --> 00:00:26.247
A good example shows both the action and the reasoning behind the action.

5
00:00:26.247 --> 00:00:29.579
Example-problem pairs are a practical design pattern.

6
00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:36.245
Learners study a worked example, then solve a similar problem with enough variation to require attention.

7
00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:41.661
This helps them compare the structure of the example with their own attempt.

8
00:00:41.661 --> 00:00:45.411
Feedback then connects the attempt back to the pattern.

9
00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:50.410
Over time, this builds a bridge from guided understanding to independent performance.

10
00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:54.576
Fading guidance means gradually reducing support as learners gain capability.

11
00:00:54.576 --> 00:00:57.492
Early practice may include fully worked examples.

12
00:00:57.492 --> 00:01:02.075
Later practice may include partially completed steps, prompts, hints, or checklists.

13
00:01:02.075 --> 00:01:04.991
Eventually, learners take on the whole task.

14
00:01:04.991 --> 00:01:12.074
The shift should be based on readiness, not on an arbitrary desire to make the course harder.

15
00:01:12.074 --> 00:01:16.240
Removing support too early can increase load without improving learning.

16
00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.156
Practice should change as learners gain experience.

17
00:01:19.156 --> 00:01:21.656
Beginners need structure, examples, and feedback.

18
00:01:21.656 --> 00:01:26.239
More advanced learners need challenge, variation, and opportunities to make decisions.

19
00:01:26.239 --> 00:01:37.070
The design problem is balancing support and challenge so learners are not left guessing at the beginning and are not trapped in over-explained exercises later.

20
00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:43.320
Good practice helps learners build schemas, test them, and use them under increasingly realistic conditions.
